From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:26:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Linux host: a damaged ELF module, manifest or NSO is a
 ModuleError, the same one every time (#13)

elf_module.py let struct.error, ValueError, KeyError, AttributeError, TypeError, MemoryError
and SystemExit out of the reader for a program header table past the file, a dynamic
section or a relocation or symbol table past the image, a symbol name outside the image,
a manifest that is not an object or lacks a field, an elf field that names another folder,
a damaged NSO and a size field in the gigabytes. Each is now a ModuleError that names the
file, field or address. The image size is capped by MAX_IMAGE (1 GiB). Nothing that loaded
before is refused except those cases: a name that is not UTF-8 keeps its bytes as \xNN.

test_elf_module_errors.py: one case per failure, a sweep over every truncation of an ELF
and a sweep over every damaged byte of the headers and tables (2140 cases), all allowing
only ModuleError and checking that a second attempt gives the same message.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: A damaged module, manifest or NSO stops the loader with one named ModuleError instead of a traceback or a process exit
Issue: Sunshine-Off/NX2Linux#13

---
